      {
        "claim": "Guildford surgeon John Howard delivered the specimens, a report of 19 November 1726 counted nine creatures, and the King sent his own surgeons including Cyriacus Ahlers.",
        "segment_index": 1,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "89% of the claim's wording appears in the reference article, including 2 number(s)",
        "correction": null,
        "method": "wikipedia-lexical"
      },
      {
        "claim": "Ahlers arrived on 20 November 1726, suspected a hoax, and found dung in one rabbit containing corn, hay and straw, which pointed away from a birth.",
