        "note": "69% of the claim's wording appears in the reference article, including 2 number(s)",
        "correction": null,
        "method": "wikipedia-lexical"
      },
      {
        "claim": "On 4 December 1726 Thomas Onslow discovered that Toft's husband had been buying young rabbits, and Toft confessed on 7 December 1726.",
        "segment_index": 3,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "Wikipedia: on 4 December Thomas Onslow, 2nd Baron Onslow, discovered Joshua Toft buying young rabbits, and a porter confessed to a bribe the same day; Toft confessed on 7 December before Manningham and Douglas.",
        "correction": null,
